      "chapter": "Matrices & Determinants",
      "question": "\\(A\\) is a square matrix of order 3 and \\(|A| = 4\\). What is \\(|\\text{adj}\\,A|\\)?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "\\(64\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "\\(16\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "\\(8\\)"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "\\(4\\)"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "B",
      "step": "For order \\(n\\), \\(|\\text{adj}\\,A| = |A|^{n-1}\\), so \\(|\\text{adj}\\,A| = 4^{2} = 16\\).",
      "checked": "A·adj A = |A| I → |A|·|adj A| = |A|³ → |adj A| = |A|² = 16. Matches the bank (B)."
